# Vercel's CLI does not reliably respect .gitignore for env files during
# `vercel deploy` uploads — it uploads .env by default and only warns
# ("Detected .env file, it is strongly recommended to use Vercel's env
# handling instead"). Environment variables are configured via `vercel env
# add` instead (see DEPLOYMENT.md), so the local .env file must never be
# part of the uploaded deployment source.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
